# Required Field Indicator Pattern

**CRITICAL: Never use manual `<span class="text-danger">*</span>` for required field indicators.**

## Correct Pattern

```html
<label for="field_name" class="required-label">Field Name</label>
<input name="field_name" id="field_name" class="form-control required">
```

CSS adds the red asterisk automatically.

## WRONG

```html
<label for="field_name">Field Name <span class="text-danger">*</span></label>
```

## Related

- `required` class on input/select is still needed for client-side validation
- `required-label` only controls the visual asterisk
